"id\": \"12d2d28fcbab7786\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.3760840977443438, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.21233472820620544, \"vector_similarity\": 0.75816596, \"dataset_name\": \"C2Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-7443.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"8757264a8a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-7443.md\", \"location\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-7443.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 20034, \"chunk_count\": 14, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:53:51\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:10:06\", \"token_count\": 7244, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: [SRC-PR-05]\\n\\n# Pull Request: Optimize histogram reservoir (open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go#7443)\\n\\n**Canonical URL**: https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go/pull/7443  \\n\\n**Author**: dashpole  \\n\\n**Created**: 2025-10-02T13:56:40Z · **Updated**: 2025-12-15T15:00:11Z  \\n\\n**Collected**: 2026-07-14T14:35:41Z  \\n\\n**State**: merged (2025-12-15T14:59:34Z)  \\n\\n**Branch**: `optimize_histogram_reservoir` → `main`  \\n\\n**Changes**: +173 / -61 across 8 files  \\n\\n**Labels**: —  \\n\\n**Milestone**: v1.40.0\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nThis improves the concurrent performance of the histogram reservoir's Offer function by 4x (i.e. 75% reduction).\\n\\nAccomplish this by locking each measurement, rather than locking around the entire storage.  Also, defer extracting the trace context from context.Context until collection time. This improves the performance of Offer, which is on the measure hot path.  Exemplars are often overwritten, so deferring the operation until Collect reduces the overall work.\\n\\n```\\n\\n                           │   main.txt   │              hist.txt              │\\n\\n                           │    sec/op    │   sec/op     vs base               │\\n\\nFixedSizeReservoirOffer-24    211.4n ± 3%   177.5n ± 3%  -16.04% (p=0.002 n=6)\\n\\nHistogramReservoirOffer-24   200.85n ± 2%   47.41n ± 2%  -76.40% (p=0.002 n=6)\\n\\ngeomean                       206.1n        91.73n       -55.48%\\n\\n```\\n\\nBenchmarks for Measure:\\n\\n```\\n\\n                                                                                 │  main.txt   │             histres.txt             │\\n\\n                                                                                 │   sec/op    │    sec/op     vs base               │\\n\\nSyncMeasure/NoView/ExemplarsEnabled/Int64Histogram/Attributes/0-24                 436.7n ± 4%   114.8n ±  5%  -73.72% (p=0.002 n=6)\\n\\nSyncMeasure/NoView/ExemplarsEnabled/Int64Histogram/Attributes/10-24                472.2n ± 2%   169.7n ±  8%  -64.08% (p=0.002 n=6)\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src pr 05 pull request optim histogram reservoir open telemetri opentelemetri go 7443 canon url http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go pull 7443 author dashpol creat 2025 10 02t13 56 40z updat 2025 12 15t15 00 11z collect 2026 07 14t14 35 41z state merg 2025 12 15t14 59 34z branch optim _ histogram _ reservoir main chang 173 61 across 8 file label mileston v1 400 descript this improv the concurr perform of the histogram reservoir s offer function by 4x i e 75 reduct accomplish this by lock each measur rather than lock around the entir storag also defer extract the trace context from context context until collect time this improv the perform of offer which is on the measur hot path exemplar are often overwritten so defer the oper until collect reduc the overal work main txt hist txt sec op sec op v base fixedsizereservoiroff 24 211 4n 3 177 5n 316 04 p 0 002 n 6 histogramreservoiroff 24 200 85n 247 41n 2 76 40 p 0 002 n 6 geomean 206 1n 91 73n 55 48 benchmark for measur main txt histr txt sec op sec op v base syncmeasur noview exemplarsen int64histogram attribut 0 24 436 7n 4 114 8n 5 73 72 p 0 002 n 6 syncmeasur noview exemplarsen int64histogram attribut 1024 472 2n 2 169 7n 8 64 08 p 0 002 n 6\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"8757264a8a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-7443.md\", \"id\": \"bcdaee6c0a13a293\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.3760166097443438, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.21233472820620544, \"vector_similarity\": 0.757941, \"dataset_name\": \"C2Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-7443.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"8757264a8a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-7443.md\", \"location\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-7443.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 20034, \"chunk_count\": 14, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:53:51\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:10:06\", \"token_count\": 7244, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: [SRC-PR-06]\\n\\n# Pull Request: Use sync.Map and atomics for fixed bucket histograms (open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go#7474)\\n\\n**Canonical URL**: https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go/pull/7474  \\n\\n**Author**: dashpole  \\n\\n**Created**: 2025-10-08T14:31:21Z · **Updated**: 2025-12-11T16:56:31Z  \\n\\n**Collected**: 2026-07-14T14:35:41Z  \\n\\n**State**: merged (2025-12-11T16:56:04Z)  \\n\\n**Branch**: `optimize_syncmap_histogram` → `main`  \\n\\n**Changes**: +560 / -201 across 7 files  \\n\\n**Labels**: —  \\n\\n**Milestone**: v1.40.0\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nImplement a lockless histogram using atomics, and use a sync.Map for attribute access.  This improves performance by ~2x.\\n\\nThe design is very similar to https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go/pull/7427, but with one additional change to make the histogram data point itself atomic:\\n\\n* For cumulative histograms, which do not use a hot/cold limitedSyncMap, we use a hot/cold data point.  This way, we maintain the keys in the sync map, but still ensure that collection gets a consistent view of measure() calls.\\n\\nParallel benchmarks:\\n\\n```\\n\\n                                                                       │  main.txt   │              hist.txt              │\\n\\n                                                                       │   sec/op    │   sec/op     vs base               │\\n\\nSyncMeasure/NoView/ExemplarsDisabled/Int64Histogram/Attributes/10-24     274.5n ± 2%   125.2n ± 5%  -54.42% (p=0.002 n=6)\\n\\nSyncMeasure/NoView/ExemplarsDisabled/Float64Histogram/Attributes/10-24   274.1n ± 2%   132.5n ± 2%  -51.65% (p=0.002 n=6)\\n\\ngeomean                                                                  274.3n        128.8n       -53.05%\\n\\n```\\n\\nzero memory allocations before and after this change for Measure().  Omitted for brevity\\n\\nBenchmarks for collect:\\n\\n```\\n\\n                                                    │   main.txt    │               hist.txt               │\\n\\n                                                    │    sec/op     │    sec/op     vs base                │\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src pr 06 pull request use sync map and atom for fix bucket histogram open telemetri opentelemetri go 7474 canon url http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go pull 7474 author dashpol creat 2025 10 08t14 31 21z updat 2025 12 11t16 56 31z collect 2026 07 14t14 35 41z state merg 2025 12 11t16 56 04z branch optim _ syncmap _ histogram main chang 560 201 across 7 file label mileston v1 400 descript implement a lockless histogram use atom and use a sync map for attribut access this improv perform by 2x the design is veri similar to http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go pull 7427 but with one addit chang to make the histogram data point itself atom for cumul histogram which do not use a hot cold limitedsyncmap we use a hot cold data point this way we maintain the key in the sync map but still ensur that collect get a consist view of measur call parallel benchmark main txt hist txt sec op sec op v base syncmeasur noview exemplarsdis int64histogram attribut 1024 274 5n 2 125 2n 5 54 42 p 0 002 n 6 syncmeasur noview exemplarsdis float64histogram attribut 1024 274 1n 2 132 5n 2 51 65 p 0 002 n 6 geomean 274 3n 128 8n 53 05 zero memori alloc befor and after this chang for measur omit for breviti benchmark for collect main txt hist txt sec op sec op v base\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"875d9f208a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-7474.md\", \"id\": \"432d9a43e09b0cb1\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.3753413577443438, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.21233472820620544, \"vector_similarity\": 0.75569016, \"dataset_name\": \"C2Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-7474.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"875d9f208a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-7474.md\", \"location\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-7474.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 32141, \"chunk_count\": 21, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:53:51\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:10:06\", \"token_count\": 11686, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}], \"pagination\": {\"page\": 1, \"page_size\": 10, \"total_chunks\": 70, \"total_pages\": 7}, \"query_info\": {\"question\": \"\\\"Tag: `v1.40.0`\\\" \\\"Published\\\" \\\"open